**ZEISS in India**

ZEISS in India is headquartered in Bengaluru and present in the fields of Industrial Quality Solutions, Research Microscopy Solutions, Medical Technology, Vision Care and Sports & Cine Optics.

ZEISS India has 3 production facilities, R&D center, Global IT services and about 40 Sales & Service offices in almost all Tier I and Tier II cities in India. With 2200+ employees and continued investments over 25 years in India, ZEISS’ success story in India is continuing at a rapid pace.

Further information at ZEISS India .

* Act as Technical Product Owner for the implementation, rollout, maintenance, and continuous improvement of Veeva QMS capabilities within VISION
* Translate business requirements from Quality Management, Manufacturing, Laboratory, Regulatory, and GxP-relevant stakeholders into clear functional and technical product backlog items

**1. Education / Professional Certification**

University degree in Business Informatics, Computer Science, Engineering, Quality Management, Life Sciences, Business Administration, or an equivalent qualification.  



**2. Experience**

More than 10 years of relevant professional experience in SAP QM, LIMS, QMS systems, quality process digitalization, or regulated system implementation within healthcare, pharmaceutical, medical device, or other GxP-relevant environments; experience with Veeva QMS is strongly preferred.  



**1. Knowledge / Skills / Other characteristics**

* + Strong functional and technical understanding of Quality Management processes and systems, preferably including Veeva QMS, SAP QM, LIMS, and related enterprise platforms;
  + Proven experience as Product Owner, Business Process Owner, Solution Lead, or Senior Business Expert in global QMS, ERP, or laboratory system implementation programs;
  + Experience with end-to-end implementation activities including requirements engineering, solution design, backlog management, configuration support, testing, validation, deployment, and hypercare;
  + Good understanding of regulated environments, computerized system validation, GxP expectations, data integrity principles, quality compliance requirements, and relevant certification standards such as ISO 13485 and MDSAP;
  + Ability to read, understand, and interpret regulatory and quality requirements and translate them into practical business processes, system requirements, and implementation priorities;
  + Ability to connect business process needs with technical solution capabilities and to communicate effectively with both business and IT stakeholders;
  + Experience in integrating QMS processes with SAP QM, MES, LIMS, document management, training, and reporting solutions is an advantage;
  + Structured, analytical, and result-oriented working style with the ability to manage complexity, dependencies, and multiple stakeholder expectations in an international environment;
  + Excellent English communication skills, both spoken and written; German or other languages are an advantage.

Your ZEISS Recruiting Team:

Itishree Pani

**Company Description**
Eurofins Scientific is an international life sciences company which provides a unique range of analytical testing services to clients across multiple industries. The Group believes it is the world leader in food, environment and pharmaceutical products testing and in agroscience CRO services. It is also one of the global independent market leaders in certain testing and laboratory services for genomics, discovery pharmacology, forensics, advanced material sciences and for supporting clinical studies. In addition, Eurofins is one of the key emerging players in specialty clinical diagnostic testing in Europe and the USA.


Group's key figures are approx. 7.296 billion Euros turnover, over 950 laboratories across 59 countries and about 65,000 staff.


**Job Description**
**Job description:**

* Act as a functional expert to collect, challenge and agree on business requirements for digitalizing business processes;
* Translate business requirements/processes into functional specifications and give detailed judgement on business complexity to promote simplification;
* Act as a product owner for the business processes and be responsible for the communication and cooperation between business and IT development teams;
* Write and maintain best practice documentation and train administrators and key users;
* Ensure level 2 support during transition life cycle (deployment) and level 3 support during operational life cycle;
* Audit and review use of the new tools to ensure implementation of best practice processes;
* Model the requirements into user stories (work items for development team) with the appropriate set of artefacts.

**EVOLUTION:**
*(for publication on Eurofins website and career portals)*
**What We Offer**

* The opportunity to grow your functional analysis skills in a demanding, fast growing organization.
* A chance to become part of an international team of professionals, working on a strategic and highly visible program.

**QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE REQUIRED:**
*(maximum 500 characters (not including spaces) for short position posting and for posting on Eurofins website and career portals)*
**Profile Description**

* Self-motivated, professional team player with customer focus;
* Affinity with and good understanding of IT concepts and digital technologies;
* Attention to detail, assertive.
* University degree in Business Engineering, Computer Science or similar educational background;
* Efficient time management and high quality attitude;
* Experience in agile development methods (scrum), preferably using Azure DevOps;
* Preferable: experience with workflows and related IT solutions.

**Qualifications**
**Requirements:**

* 6+ years of experience in analysing, describing and challenging processes and workflows;
* Knowledge of UML and other tool to create diagrams, tools to create wireframes
* Master’s degree in business administration / commercial sciences / computer sciences;
* Excellent analytical and problem solving skills;
* Excellent English language skills;
* Knowledge of service oriented software architecture;

Excellent verbal/written communication skills
